#
# `:existsOptionalPadding`/`:notExistsOptionalPadding` fixture: two `:p` facts and
# DELIBERATELY no `:q` fact at all. `FILTER EXISTS { OPTIONAL { ?x :q ?y } }` is a
# tautology regardless of `:q` data — `OPTIONAL` never empties the unit row it is
# applied to, so `EXISTS` sees a non-empty inner bag either way. The absence of any
# `:q` triple here is what makes the case discriminating: an engine that (wrongly)
# treats a group whose sole element is `OPTIONAL { P }` as equivalent to `P` itself
# would find zero matches and wrongly answer `EXISTS` false / `NOT EXISTS` true.
@prefix : <https://example.org/exists#> .

:s1 :p :o1 .
:s2 :p :o2 .
